1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,204
A mixer whirs up to speed.

2
00:00:02,204 --> 00:00:04,894
A potter's wheel spins
faster with each kick.

3
00:00:04,894 --> 00:00:06,887
A giant wheel slows to a stop.

4
00:00:07,287 --> 00:00:10,076
In each one, the turning
itself keeps changing.

5
00:00:10,526 --> 00:00:13,083
At home, Aarav switches
on the ceiling fan.

6
00:00:13,083 --> 00:00:16,087
It starts slowly, then
speeds up for a few seconds.

7
00:00:16,437 --> 00:00:19,661
How many turns does it make
before it reaches full speed?

8
00:00:19,661 --> 00:00:21,504
Can we know, without counting?

9
00:00:22,004 --> 00:00:22,904
Yes.

10
00:00:22,519 --> 00:00:24,267
With angular acceleration.

11
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:29,855
Angular acceleration, alpha, tells
how fast omega changes: the change in

12
00:00:29,855 --> 00:00:32,019
omega, divided by the time.

13
00:00:32,369 --> 00:00:35,108
Its unit is radians per second squared.

14
00:00:35,508 --> 00:00:38,668
For a fixed axis, alpha
lies along the axis too.

15
00:00:38,668 --> 00:00:41,630
Speeding up, it points
the same way as omega.

16
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:43,705
Slowing down, the opposite way.

17
00:00:44,105 --> 00:00:48,644
And every point of a rigid body has
the same alpha, just like the same

18
00:00:48,644 --> 00:00:49,544
omega.

19
00:00:49,852 --> 00:00:51,446
To the motion notebook.

20
00:00:51,446 --> 00:00:53,847
A fan, seen from below, at rest.

21
00:00:53,847 --> 00:00:54,747
Switch on.

22
00:00:55,043 --> 00:00:57,829
Alpha is four radians per second squared.

23
00:00:57,829 --> 00:01:00,298
Every second, omega grows by four.

24
00:01:00,698 --> 00:01:03,800
On the graph, omega
climbs in a straight line.

25
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:05,200
The slope is alpha.

26
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:10,659
At five seconds, omega reaches twenty
radians per second, and stays there.

27
00:01:11,059 --> 00:01:14,378
The gold area under the
line is the angle turned.

28
00:01:14,378 --> 00:01:17,063
Fifty radians in the first five seconds.

29
00:01:17,063 --> 00:01:18,401
About eight turns.

30
00:01:18,901 --> 00:01:19,914
Slow-mo replay.

31
00:01:19,914 --> 00:01:21,420
Freeze at two seconds.

32
00:01:21,770 --> 00:01:22,894
Omega is eight.

33
00:01:22,894 --> 00:01:27,458
The blade tip, zero point six metres
out, moves at four point eight metres

34
00:01:27,458 --> 00:01:28,358
per second.

35
00:01:28,734 --> 00:01:31,128
Alpha is the same for the whole fan.

36
00:01:31,128 --> 00:01:34,355
But the tip speeds up along
its circle by r alpha.

37
00:01:34,355 --> 00:01:36,928
Two point four metres per second squared.

38
00:01:37,528 --> 00:01:40,036
Now switch it off, and it slows down.

39
00:01:40,036 --> 00:01:43,357
Does alpha point the same
way as omega, or opposite?

40
00:01:43,357 --> 00:01:44,554
Pause and decide.

41
00:01:47,654 --> 00:01:48,554
Opposite!

42
00:01:48,342 --> 00:01:50,937
Omega keeps its direction, but it shrinks.

43
00:01:50,937 --> 00:01:52,846
So alpha points the other way.

44
00:01:52,846 --> 00:01:55,125
On the graph, the line slopes down.

45
00:01:55,725 --> 00:01:56,661
Now the equations.

46
00:01:56,661 --> 00:01:58,399
They are old friends in new clothes.

47
00:01:58,749 --> 00:01:59,661
Step one.

48
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:03,846
Alpha is d omega by d t,
just as a is d v by d t.

49
00:02:04,596 --> 00:02:05,496
Step two.

50
00:02:05,483 --> 00:02:09,820
With a steady alpha, omega
equals omega nought plus alpha t.

51
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:11,897
Like v equals u plus a t.

52
00:02:12,647 --> 00:02:13,565
Step three.

53
00:02:13,565 --> 00:02:16,500
The angle is the area
under the omega line.

54
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:20,193
Theta equals omega nought t,
plus half alpha t squared.

55
00:02:20,943 --> 00:02:21,843
Step four.

56
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:26,667
Remove t, and you get omega squared
equals omega nought squared, plus two

57
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:27,667
alpha theta.

58
00:02:28,417 --> 00:02:29,408
Remember this.

59
00:02:29,408 --> 00:02:32,611
Swap x for theta, v for
omega, and a for alpha.

60
00:02:32,611 --> 00:02:34,842
The same equations work for turning.

61
00:02:35,542 --> 00:02:38,728
Why does the blade tip speed
up more than the middle?

62
00:02:38,728 --> 00:02:39,694
Link by link.

63
00:02:40,044 --> 00:02:42,587
The whole blade turns as one piece.

64
00:02:42,587 --> 00:02:46,263
So every point has the same
omega, at every moment.

65
00:02:46,663 --> 00:02:50,421
So omega changes by the
same amount for every point.

66
00:02:50,421 --> 00:02:51,423
Same alpha.

67
00:02:51,823 --> 00:02:53,435
But speed is r omega.

68
00:02:53,435 --> 00:02:55,883
So the change in speed is r alpha.

69
00:02:55,883 --> 00:02:58,875
The tip, farther out, gains speed fastest.

70
00:02:59,475 --> 00:03:00,537
Side by side.

71
00:03:00,537 --> 00:03:04,842
A bike speeds up at two metres per
second squared for five seconds.

72
00:03:04,842 --> 00:03:07,918
Ten metres per second,
and twenty five metres.

73
00:03:08,318 --> 00:03:12,319
The fan: four radians per
second squared for five seconds.

74
00:03:12,319 --> 00:03:16,528
It reaches twenty radians per
second, and turns fifty radians.

75
00:03:17,128 --> 00:03:18,187
Now you try.

76
00:03:18,187 --> 00:03:22,639
Fan A goes from zero to twenty
radians per second in five seconds.

77
00:03:22,639 --> 00:03:25,240
Fan B, from ten to thirty in five.

78
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:27,193
Which has the bigger alpha?

79
00:03:27,193 --> 00:03:28,509
Pause and decide.

80
00:03:31,709 --> 00:03:32,609
The same!

81
00:03:32,498 --> 00:03:36,415
Both gain twenty in five seconds,
so alpha is four for both.

82
00:03:36,415 --> 00:03:39,139
It depends on the change, not the speed.

83
00:03:39,789 --> 00:03:41,463
Now, one worked example.

84
00:03:41,463 --> 00:03:42,363
Aarav's fan.

85
00:03:42,673 --> 00:03:46,883
From rest, it reaches twenty
radians per second in five seconds.

86
00:03:46,883 --> 00:03:49,453
Find alpha, and the number of turns.

87
00:03:49,953 --> 00:03:52,886
Omega equals omega nought plus alpha t.

88
00:03:52,886 --> 00:03:55,930
Twenty equals zero plus alpha times five.

89
00:03:55,930 --> 00:03:57,430
So alpha is four.

90
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:00,630
Theta equals half alpha t squared.

91
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:03,080
Half of four, times twenty five.

92
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,215
Fifty radians.

93
00:04:04,965 --> 00:04:07,097
One turn is two pi radians.

94
00:04:07,097 --> 00:04:09,001
So fifty, over two pi.

95
00:04:09,751 --> 00:04:12,053
That is about seven point nine six.

96
00:04:12,053 --> 00:04:14,393
Nearly eight turns before full speed.

97
00:04:15,043 --> 00:04:16,505
Now, the exam trap.

98
00:04:16,855 --> 00:04:20,648
Many students find theta equals
fifty, and say: fifty turns.

99
00:04:21,048 --> 00:04:23,387
But theta comes out in radians.

100
00:04:23,387 --> 00:04:24,838
Divide by two pi.

101
00:04:24,838 --> 00:04:27,730
Fifty radians is only about eight turns.

102
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:29,828
Where is this asked?

103
00:04:29,828 --> 00:04:34,397
In wheels that speed up or brake,
angles and turns in a given time, and

104
00:04:34,397 --> 00:04:35,690
with torque later.

105
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:37,479
Exam level now.

106
00:04:37,479 --> 00:04:41,997
A wheel speeds up steadily from ten
to thirty radians per second, while

107
00:04:41,997 --> 00:04:44,054
turning through eighty radians.

108
00:04:44,054 --> 00:04:46,332
Find alpha, and the time taken.

109
00:04:46,332 --> 00:04:47,573
Pause and solve.

110
00:04:52,973 --> 00:04:54,253
The answer is B.

111
00:04:54,253 --> 00:04:57,321
Alpha is five, and the
time is four seconds.

112
00:04:57,821 --> 00:05:02,446
Use omega squared equals omega
nought squared plus two alpha theta.

113
00:05:02,446 --> 00:05:06,180
Nine hundred equals one
hundred plus one sixty alpha.

114
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:09,479
So eight hundred equals one sixty alpha.

115
00:05:09,479 --> 00:05:12,331
Alpha is five radians per second squared.

116
00:05:12,831 --> 00:05:16,079
Then omega equals omega
nought plus alpha t.

117
00:05:16,079 --> 00:05:18,417
Thirty equals ten plus five t.

118
00:05:18,417 --> 00:05:20,190
So t is four seconds.

119
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:22,330
Here is your recap.

120
00:05:22,330 --> 00:05:23,913
Screenshot this card.

121
00:05:27,113 --> 00:05:29,051
Can you answer these without help?

122
00:05:29,451 --> 00:05:30,351
One.

123
00:05:29,917 --> 00:05:33,442
What does an alpha of four
radians per second squared mean?

124
00:05:34,342 --> 00:05:35,242
Two.

125
00:05:34,785 --> 00:05:37,106
When does alpha point opposite to omega?

126
00:05:38,006 --> 00:05:38,906
Three.

127
00:05:38,532 --> 00:05:41,427
Why must you divide theta
by two pi to get turns?

128
00:05:42,327 --> 00:05:45,652
Next time: why are door handles
always far from the hinge?

129
00:05:45,652 --> 00:05:46,655
We meet torque.
